Nitpick but a two-case switch inside an if for the same value seems a bit convoluted, it could just be:
```cpp
if (res == -1) {
	return ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND;
} else if (res <= 0) {
	return ERR_FILE_CANT_OPEN;
}
```
(assuming that it can actually be < -1)

But that's mostly a matter of taste I guess, it's fine to keep as is if you prefer it so.
